Tips.

The tip on a bill (money) at a rate (a whole number) is money:
the bill times the rate divided by 100 rounded to 2 places.

The total with tip of a bill (money) at a rate (a whole number) is money:
the bill plus the tip on the bill at the rate.

For example, the tip on 40 at 15 is 6.
For example, the tip on 33.33 at 10 is 3.33.
For example, the total with tip of 50 at 20 is 60.
